{# Bubble rise layer (LAB-504) — decorative sprites that float up as the
   reader scrolls down, completing the "descend below the water" metaphor
   (LAB-461): you sink, the bubbles stream past on their way up.

   Pure decoration: aria-hidden, pointer-events: none, and every sprite is
   parked below the viewport at rest — only the scroll-driven rise animation
   (main.css motion section) ever brings one on screen, so reduced-motion
   users, browsers without scroll timelines, and non-scrolling pages simply
   never see them.

   Sprites are plain <img> elements: swapping the artwork (e.g. for the stock
   set's transparent PNGs, should the owner download them from Freepik) is a
   src swap — no CSS involved. Per-bubble lane/size/speed knobs live in the
   .bubble:nth-child rules in main.css (inline style would trip
   html-validate's no-inline-style gate), keyed to the ORDER of this list —
   add or remove a sprite here and the nth-child ladder must follow. #}
<div class="bubble-field" aria-hidden="true">
  <img class="bubble" src="/assets/images/bubbles/bubble-mini.svg" alt="" width="120" height="120">
  <img class="bubble" src="/assets/images/bubbles/bubble-iris.svg" alt="" width="120" height="120">
  <img class="bubble" src="/assets/images/bubbles/bubble-aqua.svg" alt="" width="120" height="120">
  <img class="bubble" src="/assets/images/bubbles/bubble-mini.svg" alt="" width="120" height="120">
  <img class="bubble" src="/assets/images/bubbles/bubble-mini.svg" alt="" width="120" height="120">
  <img class="bubble" src="/assets/images/bubbles/bubble-pearl.svg" alt="" width="120" height="120">
  <img class="bubble" src="/assets/images/bubbles/bubble-aqua.svg" alt="" width="120" height="120">
  <img class="bubble" src="/assets/images/bubbles/bubble-iris.svg" alt="" width="120" height="120">
</div>
